If the right injection of a set V is a neighbourhood of the separated sum Aⁿ + Aⁿ, then V is a neighbourhood of the n-fold power of A.

The membership splits into the sum master, a left summand, or a right summand. The master case is impossible because the basepoint belongs to the master and not to a right injection. The left case takes a nonempty witness from apowNe and produces a left-injection token, which cannot lie in a right injection. The right case uses injectivity of the right injection.
